test/check/error-default.sumspec:12:16:
   |
12 | Mode __default Maybe = On | Off        -- not a variant
   |                ^
Maybe is not a variant here; Mode's default is one of its variants, such as On

test/check/error-default.sumspec:13:22:
   |
13 | Zoom = Int __default "big"             -- a string on an __int
   |                      ^
Zoom is an __int, so "big" doesn't fit it

test/check/error-default.sumspec:14:24:
   |
14 | Label = Name __default 3               -- an integer on a __text
   |                        ^
Label is a __text, so 3 doesn't fit it

test/check/error-default.sumspec:15:6:
   |
15 | Pair __default On = Mode * Zoom         -- a product
   |      ^
Pair is a product, so it takes no default: a factor left out takes its own type's; give the default to the factor's type

test/check/error-default.sumspec:16:16:
   |
16 | Items = [Mode] __default Off           -- a list
   |                ^
Items is a list, so it takes no default; a list left out may hold any elements

test/check/error-default.sumspec:17:12:
   |
17 | At = Stamp __default 0                 -- an atomic with no base
   |            ^
At is an atomic with no base, so no value of it is written; it has no default

test/check/error-default.sumspec:18:17:
   |
18 | Level __default 2 = Low | High         -- a literal on a sum
   |                 ^
Level is a sum, so its default is one of its variants, such as Low

test/check/error-default.sumspec:19:23:
   |
19 | Other = Int __default Big              -- a constant of another type
   |                       ^
Big is a constant of Zoom, so it isn't a default of Other

test/check/error-default.sumspec:20:23:
   |
20 | Course __default Auto.Fast             -- a dot after a named payload
   |                       ^
a default picks a variant inside an inline sum only, and Fast comes after a variant whose payload isn't one

test/check/error-default.sumspec:24:22:
   |
24 | Size = Int __default Large             -- no such constant
   |                      ^
Size is an __int, so its default is a literal or a constant of Size; there's no constant Large

